===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|fro|tartre}}, from {{der|en|ML.|tartarum}}, from {{der|en|gkm|τάρταρον}}, said to be from {{der|en|ar|دُرْدِيّ}}, from {{der|ar|fa|درد||durd}} ''dregs'', from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*dʰreyd-}}; see ''{{l|en|dirt}}''. Please note that it is already found in {{w|lang=en|Pelagonius}}’s ''Ars veterinaria'' 46 in the adjective {{m|la|tartarālis}}, if the reading is correct.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[red]] [[compound]] [[deposited]] during [[wine]] [[making]]; mostly [[potassium]] [[hydrogen]] [[tartrate]] — a source of [[cream of tartar]].
# A [[hard]] [[yellow]] [[deposit]] on the [[tooth|teeth]], formed from [[dental]] [[plaque]].

